# Lantern enemy-animation handoff · 7 October 2026

Seven selected groups, 14 clips, 90 distinct drawings. This small index refers to the existing source/runtime archives; it contains no artwork and changes no delivered assets. The six registered Monk defeat PNGs are an alternate placement of existing drawings, not six new drawings.

## Import boundary

- All assets are one-facing TESTS: world +X / screen-down-right. None is game-integrated or certified for exact camera, contacts, seamless state transitions or production readiness.
- `catalog.json` is an informational summary, not a drop-in engine schema. Keep original metadata authoritative. File paths resolve from `lantern_enemy_animations_20261007/`; exact ZIP member paths are also supplied. Extract each archive pair into its own group directory because ZIP wrapper folders differ and several archives have no wrapper.
- Preserve delivered source rasters, native pixels and fixed canvases. Do not auto-fit/center each pose to its bounds or upscale during source preparation. No mirrored or interpolated drawings are included. Runtime mirroring or guarded motion warping can be tested separately for lighting, identity, props and artifacts, without baking destructive changes into the masters. Respect documented extraction/alpha cleanup and integer registration. Pivots are authoring/review coordinates. Pixels-per-world-unit and calibrated observed ground anchors remain null.
- All exposures use integer 60 Hz ticks, not 60 unique drawings per second. Review-video repetition is separate from runtime looping. Spell effects are baked in; cue/event metadata does not implement gameplay.

